LRC loneliness tournament gauges (codex-2026-06-01-S507)
sample grid: t=a/840, a=1..839

Tournament Analysis declaration
  vertices: moving runners in the speed set
  target: normalized loneliness depth (k+1)*min_i ||s_i t||
  tie Hamiltonian path: increasing speed/index order
  gauges:
    half_turn                i beats j when j lies in i's trailing/leading semicircle; the S26 1/2 meter.
    theta_close_switch       reverse the base path on pairs closer than 2/(k+1).
    antipodal_open_switch    reverse the base path on pairs within 1/(k+1) of antipodal separation.
    unsafe_dominance         a runner inside the forbidden origin interval beats a safe runner; ties use half-turn.
    safe_dominance           a safe runner beats an unsafe runner; ties use half-turn.
    lrc_band_dominance       comfortable-safe beats near-safe beats unsafe; equal bands use half-turn.
    endpoint_wall_pressure   runner nearer the LRC endpoint wall ||st||=1/(k+1) wins; ties use half-turn.
    origin_bracket_flip      flip half-turn on pairs bracketing the origin inside the 2/(k+1) corridor.
    same_side_escape         on one side of the origin, farther runner wins; opposite-side pairs use half-turn.
    relief_bottleneck        runner whose deletion most improves the current lonely distance wins.

