Interpretation
  1. Pure half-turn remains a spread/1/2-gap meter, not an LRC-safe meter.
  2. Unsafe/safe dominance turns the score sequence into a coarse LRC
     witness detector: zero unsafe runners becomes a visible block event.
  3. Theta-close and antipodal-open switches are the best shape-only
     candidates: weaker than status dominance, but less tautological and
     especially good on the mixed-7 case.
  4. LRC band dominance records unsafe/near/deep endpoint slack, but by
     itself is a pressure diagnostic rather than a safe-witness classifier.
  5. Endpoint-wall pressure is a boundary meter rather than a witness meter:
     it spikes near ||s_i t|| = 1/(k+1), useful for corridor/peel scripts.
  6. Origin-bracket and same-side escape are shape gauges: weaker as direct
     classifiers, but they preserve pair geometry that scalar rank gauges
     erase.
